WEBVTT

00:11.360 --> 00:12.320
Hold on, Iwato!

00:13.950 --> 00:14.490
Hold on!

00:14.490 --> 00:15.820
Like hell I can!

00:15.820 --> 00:17.580
Can't you tell what time it is already?

00:17.580 --> 00:18.490
Who gives a shit about the time!

00:18.490 --> 00:21.000
I'll have that bastard Natsuiri spill everything!

00:21.500 --> 00:24.370
They're using a teammates
death as if it were some tool...

00:24.370 --> 00:27.420
I bet they're the ones who killed Emiru too!

00:27.420 --> 00:28.590
Even so...

00:28.590 --> 00:30.840
This can't end with a simple "I don't know"!

00:30.840 --> 00:32.630
I know that, but still...

00:35.050 --> 00:37.260
This is going to sound really unlike me, but...

00:37.930 --> 00:39.140
I'm scared.

00:41.060 --> 00:44.060
Scared of knowing everything that's happening.

00:44.730 --> 00:46.270
Raika.

00:46.270 --> 00:50.860
I'm aware that what I'm
saying makes no sense, but...

00:52.570 --> 00:55.660
I'm also... scared.

00:56.320 --> 01:01.660
But even so, I do want to know—or rather...

01:04.040 --> 01:13.050
The red moon was shining down on those seeking the truth, and on those fearing it.

01:13.050 --> 01:17.050
And even on those who put the truth on the table.

01:29.060 --> 01:34.650
The Dark Metal

01:29.110 --> 01:29.150
The Dark Metal

01:34.650 --> 01:39.070
Night turns to day, and day turns to night. Our wishes have wilted away

01:39.070 --> 01:43.240
Where did the person I want to meet go?

01:43.240 --> 01:47.710
Interlocking these fingers with my beloved

01:47.710 --> 01:51.460
Even though I can't feel them, I continue to live

01:51.500 --> 01:56.090
When the flower's petals

01:56.090 --> 02:00.220
Are plucked off by the wind's playful gale

02:00.220 --> 02:04.680
They are scattered in every direction

02:04.680 --> 02:10.020
Even if you long for it

02:11.020 --> 02:15.740
Don't disappear, just don't

02:15.740 --> 02:19.530
I can even give everything else away if I have to

02:19.530 --> 02:24.370
You were there, and I was there with you

02:24.370 --> 02:28.710
Let me take in these memories

02:28.710 --> 02:35.630
These brief moments are connected, turning it into eternity

02:52.520 --> 02:55.730
Episode 11
Red Lament of Cruelty

02:52.900 --> 02:54.020
No, that's okay.

02:54.020 --> 02:56.030
It doesn't matter how late it is.

02:56.030 --> 02:59.990
This is important, so I'll answer your questions.

02:59.990 --> 03:03.120
It's in regards to the second machine's LIM, correct?

03:03.120 --> 03:06.740
Emiru's whole body had already turned into Necrometal.

03:07.330 --> 03:10.210
Physically, she was already dead.

03:10.210 --> 03:13.460
But even so! Turning her into a machine...

03:13.460 --> 03:14.340
That's too cruel!

03:14.340 --> 03:15.880
Why?

03:15.880 --> 03:19.550
If she turns into a LIM,
her body won't ever go back to normal,

03:19.550 --> 03:23.260
but she can eternally escape
death in the mental sense.

03:23.760 --> 03:28.600
Besides, Emiru herself chose to become a LIM.

03:28.600 --> 03:33.730
She kept going on many times about wanting to defeat that Corpse.

03:34.190 --> 03:38.150
And we wanted to grant her that wish.

03:38.150 --> 03:40.860
We think she'd be happy about all this.

03:41.360 --> 03:42.740
Please don't decide things for her!

03:44.320 --> 03:46.410
Don't make assumptions on her feelings!

03:47.910 --> 03:49.580
Oh?

03:49.580 --> 03:52.960
You're right. It's bad to assume.

03:52.960 --> 03:55.380
You're such a noble girl, Mahmu.

03:57.250 --> 04:02.470
Sasame, what do you think was going through Emiru's mind?

04:05.010 --> 04:06.010
Well...

04:06.970 --> 04:09.390
Why are you asking her?

04:09.390 --> 04:12.350
Come over here, Sasame.

04:15.350 --> 04:18.900
I'd like to hear what your opinion is.

04:18.900 --> 04:24.030
Choosing between turning into a Necrometal and waiting to die, or turning into a LIM...

04:24.030 --> 04:26.490
What's your honest opinion?

04:28.120 --> 04:29.200
I...

04:29.200 --> 04:30.450
Stop it!

04:30.450 --> 04:31.500
Hey!

04:35.580 --> 04:41.920
Never in their wildest dreams did think they'd curse the ability to link their thoughts.

04:41.920 --> 04:46.720
It was as if a wedge was driven into a part of your own body.

04:46.720 --> 04:52.810
And from there, slowly, a hard object was creeping into the deepest parts of your body.

04:53.480 --> 04:57.440
The feeling as if a metallic ant's nest were spreading.

04:57.440 --> 05:02.030
And the person who was the source of this feeling...

05:04.570 --> 05:05.490
Sasame?

05:06.570 --> 05:09.410
Now, tell us...

05:11.080 --> 05:12.410
Sasame.

05:37.770 --> 05:39.860
A long silence passed.

05:40.570 --> 05:44.150
Shadows being born from the rays of light of the red moon.

05:44.570 --> 05:48.570
An ominous second hand that marks the passage of silent time.

05:55.620 --> 05:56.500
All right!

05:58.210 --> 06:02.840
It feels so good to move around at this hour!

06:02.840 --> 06:05.550
We really were dumb.

06:05.550 --> 06:07.050
We stopped thinking.

06:07.050 --> 06:09.550
We were told not to walk out at night and clammed up.

06:09.550 --> 06:12.260
And got told to fight and so we did.

06:15.520 --> 06:17.180
What was that for?

06:18.310 --> 06:19.560
I'm sorry.

06:20.730 --> 06:22.770
If you're gonna apologize, then—

06:22.770 --> 06:28.240
I finally realized why you were so scared of knowing the truth.

06:30.070 --> 06:36.910
No matter what the truth was, after all
that's happened, we can't let Heito and Emiru die.

06:36.910 --> 06:40.630
If our feelings waver from knowing the truth,

06:40.630 --> 06:44.250
then it's better to stay ignorant and think only about saving your teammates.

06:45.340 --> 06:46.380
Am I right?

06:51.090 --> 06:53.600
I'm just weak.

06:54.010 --> 06:58.980
Just by knowing the truth and seeing Sasame like that...

07:00.060 --> 07:01.350
I'm already so agitated.

07:06.400 --> 07:08.030
I'm glad it was you.

07:09.400 --> 07:13.910
I'm glad that you were the one who synchronized best with me.

07:13.910 --> 07:18.660
Among all the lies, I can trust that you of all people have nothing to lie about.

07:18.660 --> 07:21.210
I can feel that you alone are beautiful.

07:25.460 --> 07:27.880
Oh, don't get me wrong, and don't press your luck!

07:27.880 --> 07:29.630
I wasn't talking about looks!

07:31.010 --> 07:32.760
That was unnecessary!

07:34.470 --> 07:36.010
You're so violent...

07:37.850 --> 07:40.520
I'm also glad that it was you.

07:41.310 --> 07:42.190
Yeah!

07:51.820 --> 07:54.070
It isn't! It really isn't!

07:54.070 --> 07:57.410
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm so sorry...

08:00.870 --> 08:00.910
That's right,
it was Emiru
who was
supposedly
dead...
And yet
was not dead.
She was
alive!
With her
strong will...
Live, Live...
I want to
fight again...
Not for
revenge.

08:08.960 --> 08:10.420
This isn't it...

08:18.060 --> 08:23.640
It really isn't! I didn't want you to stay alive like this!

08:35.950 --> 08:37.450
What a shocker that was.

08:39.240 --> 08:44.330
Sasame, do you remember what we talked about on that rainy day?

08:47.960 --> 08:48.790
Yeah.

08:49.590 --> 08:52.170
This day was bound to come eventually.

08:52.920 --> 08:55.180
It was just a matter of sooner or later.

08:59.390 --> 09:00.680
Minashi-kun...

09:01.890 --> 09:04.230
W-Wait, no...

09:04.640 --> 09:06.150
N-No...

09:36.300 --> 09:39.220
This is... us.

09:39.220 --> 09:41.430
I love Akashi.

09:42.930 --> 09:44.180
Me too.

09:45.520 --> 09:49.610
Not just Akashi, but everyone else in Gargouille as well.

09:50.860 --> 09:54.320
That's why I don't want anyone to get hurt more than they are now.

09:55.690 --> 09:57.610
I understand even if you don't say it.

09:58.860 --> 10:03.540
Because we're linked deeper than anyone else.

10:11.380 --> 10:12.840
Why, Sasame?

10:14.130 --> 10:17.510
Why were you trying to bear all the pain alone?

10:17.510 --> 10:19.720
Why didn't you tell me?

10:20.550 --> 10:25.810
And why didn't I understand you at all?

10:25.810 --> 10:26.730
Dammit!

10:32.610 --> 10:33.690
Sasame!

10:33.690 --> 10:35.030
Wait!

10:35.030 --> 10:36.070
I'll go after her.

10:37.700 --> 10:41.240
Oh, there she goes.

10:41.240 --> 10:42.200
What should I do?

10:42.200 --> 10:46.830
The only person who could relay how Emiru felt is now gone.

10:46.830 --> 10:48.080
Damn you!

10:48.080 --> 10:50.790
What's your problem?

10:51.250 --> 10:56.710
You failed in the retrieval of the Sable and came sulking back.

10:56.710 --> 10:59.800
I don't want someone like that saying they damn me.

10:59.800 --> 11:00.800
Damn <i>you</i>.

11:02.260 --> 11:06.310
But you know, maybe that was going a bit too far.

11:06.310 --> 11:09.310
Choosing between dying or turning into a LIM...

11:09.310 --> 11:11.560
Maybe those two aren't the only choices.

11:12.520 --> 11:14.230
At least for a short while now...

11:14.230 --> 11:15.360
At least now?

11:15.360 --> 11:18.900
If I can do more research on that Corpse,

11:18.900 --> 11:23.120
we could find a way to stop the progression of Necrometal.

11:23.120 --> 11:25.030
Before they turn into LIMs.

11:25.030 --> 11:28.290
You want us to defeat the Corpse?

11:28.290 --> 11:34.790
It'd be impossible after she turns into a LIM,
but if it's before that then the possibility isn't zero.

11:34.790 --> 11:39.470
Pretty soon we'll be able to unveil a new weapon that specializes in facing the Corpses too.

11:40.090 --> 11:41.720
The Corpse...

11:44.470 --> 11:46.180
If I defeat the Corpse...

11:50.810 --> 11:53.600
I will crush the Corpse!

12:06.700 --> 12:08.120
Sasame...

12:12.620 --> 12:19.460
The second hand of the red moon marks the passage to times past.

12:20.630 --> 12:23.680
Sasame, what are you doing here?

12:23.680 --> 12:25.590
Oh, well...

12:25.590 --> 12:28.100
I was thinking of sleeping out here tonight.

12:28.100 --> 12:30.520
Sleeping out here?

12:30.520 --> 12:31.520
Yeah.

12:33.190 --> 12:38.440
I thought it'd be nice to sleep outside while looking at the starts instead of being in a cramped room.

12:38.440 --> 12:40.400
A cramped room...

12:44.990 --> 12:46.660
It was disgusting, wasn't it?

12:47.910 --> 12:50.330
That's not true. I...

12:53.160 --> 12:58.290
I've always felt that I wanted
to do something for everyone.

12:59.210 --> 13:02.760
However, I couldn't think of anything I could possibly do.

13:03.760 --> 13:07.850
When my body started to turn this way, I was scared at first.

13:09.140 --> 13:13.390
But thanks to that,
I found something I could do for everyone.

13:13.390 --> 13:17.020
By that, do you mean turning into a LIM?

13:20.610 --> 13:22.320
Self-sacrifice.

13:22.320 --> 13:23.530
How beautiful.

13:25.200 --> 13:29.160
You already heard there's no way back once you become a LIM, right?

13:29.160 --> 13:31.700
I know that, but...

13:31.700 --> 13:34.500
All you're doing is abandoning your right to think!

13:35.500 --> 13:39.040
Natsuiri told us that if we defeat the Corpse

13:39.040 --> 13:40.960
they might be able to cure your Necrometal corruption.

13:42.170 --> 13:46.510
We can't really trust Natsuiri, but still...

13:46.510 --> 13:50.220
Instead of lowering yourself
to become a mindless war tool,

13:50.220 --> 13:52.930
you're better off believing what he says.

13:52.930 --> 13:54.220
But...

13:56.190 --> 13:58.480
Battles don't suit you.

13:59.230 --> 14:01.360
Battles don't...

14:01.360 --> 14:04.360
You're better off being cheerful.

14:07.450 --> 14:13.950
I had never felt the emotion
of happiness until I came here.

14:15.040 --> 14:18.500
All of you gave me my happiness.

14:18.500 --> 14:23.630
So if I can save everyone from
harm by becoming a LIM...

14:23.630 --> 14:25.010
Who do you mean by everyone?!

14:25.960 --> 14:30.300
If you become a LIM, at least my...

14:30.720 --> 14:35.140
My heart could never be saved.

14:35.140 --> 14:36.480
Akashi-kun...

14:37.480 --> 14:38.890
I beg you, Sasame!

14:39.440 --> 14:40.690
Save me!

14:43.360 --> 14:44.530
Sasame...

14:48.610 --> 14:52.240
I'm smiling...

14:53.580 --> 14:54.240
The same as before.

14:55.450 --> 14:58.250
Why am I smiling?

14:59.250 --> 15:00.960
And at a time like this...

15:02.250 --> 15:04.800
Akashi-kun, you're crying.

15:06.920 --> 15:07.970
Crying?

15:09.340 --> 15:10.220
I am?

15:12.390 --> 15:15.760
I'm crying...

15:32.450 --> 15:36.450
I can feel your memories, Akashi-kun.

15:38.500 --> 15:41.620
Ah, I see.

15:43.170 --> 15:45.590
That's how it always was.

15:45.590 --> 15:48.630
Even on that day I came back from the Lightless Realm.

15:48.630 --> 15:52.470
To think he'd come back from the Lightless Realm...

15:52.470 --> 15:56.180
Does he think we abandoned him in there or something?

15:56.180 --> 15:58.850
He wouldn't think something like that.

15:58.850 --> 16:01.940
There were many families that got separated.

16:01.940 --> 16:03.310
It couldn't be helped.

16:03.310 --> 16:07.610
It's fine if that's the case,
but unlike you, he doesn't say anything.

16:08.030 --> 16:09.690
It's kinda creepy.

16:12.240 --> 16:13.240
Akashi...

16:14.410 --> 16:16.450
What's with those eyes?

16:16.450 --> 16:19.080
It's all because you wandered off on your own!

16:19.080 --> 16:20.330
Dad!

16:20.330 --> 16:23.420
A-Akashi, I have some peach cake for you.

16:23.420 --> 16:24.790
Akashi!

16:25.250 --> 16:26.790
Akashi, let's...

16:32.050 --> 16:34.550
You cry because you have a desire.

16:35.260 --> 16:37.760
A desire that's saying you want to be loved.

16:39.060 --> 16:45.020
I had already known since long ago that crying won't get you what you want.

16:45.850 --> 16:49.820
That was why I didn't know.

16:53.780 --> 16:55.780
After I lost Aoshi...

16:58.660 --> 16:59.410
Akashi!

17:01.830 --> 17:03.330
...I was sad.

17:06.710 --> 17:09.170
Thank you, Sasame.

17:09.170 --> 17:13.090
Do you know how I feel when we're like this?

17:14.470 --> 17:15.630
I don't.

17:17.220 --> 17:18.010
Yeah.

17:19.010 --> 17:22.680
But there's a scent that's very relieving.

17:22.680 --> 17:23.520
Yeah.

17:25.310 --> 17:31.110
I'll defeat the Corpse, so can you wait for me?

17:32.570 --> 17:33.360
Yeah.

17:34.280 --> 17:39.240
For the boy who was continually chased by his elder brother's shadow...

17:39.240 --> 17:41.540
That was the first warmth he felt.

17:42.290 --> 17:47.000
And that warmth was also a first for the girl.

17:47.830 --> 17:53.960
The two of them wished for this moment to last on for as long as possible.

17:55.590 --> 17:59.470
The second hand of moonlight that marks the passage to times past

17:59.470 --> 18:05.430
eventually gets eradicated by the rays of sunlight that push towards the future.

18:28.750 --> 18:30.170
Good morning!

18:32.380 --> 18:34.250
It's a wonderful morning.

18:34.250 --> 18:35.340
Did you sleep well?

18:36.170 --> 18:39.930
You weren't scared when Akashi embraced you.

18:42.510 --> 18:47.270
But you were so scared when
I embraced you, weren't you?

18:49.690 --> 18:50.980
That's all right.

18:50.980 --> 18:52.770
It's nothing to be embarrassed about.

18:53.610 --> 18:57.900
That emotion you harbor in your heart right now

18:59.240 --> 19:01.240
is the driving force for everything.

19:10.960 --> 19:12.290
Susan...

19:12.290 --> 19:13.380
I'll drive you home.

19:13.380 --> 19:15.500
There's something I'd like to ask you too.

19:17.840 --> 19:20.930
Something like that happened last night?

19:20.930 --> 19:22.010
Yeah.

19:22.010 --> 19:27.720
I was worried about Saginuma Akashi's recent comments and actions, so I tailed him.

19:28.640 --> 19:31.690
A lot of things make sense now. Including what a LIM truly is.

19:34.730 --> 19:38.030
Emiru didn't die, and neither did Aoshi.

19:39.860 --> 19:44.700
It looks like you're debating if the decision to turn people into LIMs was right or not.

19:45.240 --> 19:48.160
But that's something that'll
be decided when this is all over.

19:49.080 --> 19:53.710
At the very least, prepare yourself to bear the burden of sin.

19:54.170 --> 19:56.170
That goes for both you and me.

20:02.590 --> 20:04.590
Sweet impossibilities!

20:04.590 --> 20:06.470
You're being naive!

20:06.470 --> 20:09.270
Let you go into the Lightless Realm all alone?

20:09.270 --> 20:12.560
You think the Argent can do something alone?

20:12.560 --> 20:16.360
You think I'd authorize something so reckless?

20:16.360 --> 20:17.770
Huh? Huh?

20:18.650 --> 20:20.610
But of course I would!

20:21.070 --> 20:23.070
I love such sweetness.

20:25.160 --> 20:29.160
That's the penetrator that was fortified for anti-Corpse use.

20:29.160 --> 20:31.620
The discharger's been improved too.

20:31.620 --> 20:36.040
But don't forget that we're still in the development phase for it.

20:36.040 --> 20:37.590
I know that.

20:37.590 --> 20:41.170
The objective this time is just the recovery of Sable, right?

20:42.510 --> 20:45.180
I'll bring Heito and Emiru back.

20:46.180 --> 20:49.810
Someday, I'll also defeat that Corpse. Just me and Aoshi.

20:50.770 --> 20:54.140
That's why there's no need
for yet another new MA-Vess.

20:54.690 --> 20:55.690
Akashi...

20:56.610 --> 21:01.280
The other day you said you tried piloting the Reaper.

21:01.280 --> 21:02.570
Yes...

21:02.570 --> 21:06.070
But it didn't accept me at all.

21:07.370 --> 21:11.370
It was as if it was forbidding me from being there.

21:13.540 --> 21:17.330
I finally understand how Aoshi feels.

21:19.670 --> 21:24.930
I don't think there's a man out there who'd try to make his loved ones fight.

21:26.720 --> 21:30.890
I'm sure Akashi wanted to protect you, Kasane-san.

21:33.430 --> 21:35.940
Someone has to do it.

21:35.940 --> 21:37.940
I'll make sure I come back.

21:45.780 --> 21:46.990
Kasane-san?

22:01.590 --> 22:03.960
She cries just like a child.

22:06.760 --> 22:09.890
The Argent is entering the Lightless Realm.

22:10.390 --> 22:13.600
You were crying too, Aoshi.

22:13.600 --> 22:16.060
You didn't want to die.

22:16.060 --> 22:18.140
Such a disgraceful plea for your life.

22:18.350 --> 22:21.400
But I understand how you felt...

22:22.190 --> 22:25.490
That's because I don't want to die now either.

22:26.240 --> 22:30.030
Because there's someone waiting for me to return.

22:44.840 --> 22:55.470
Throwing away all my excuses, I traced over my abrased heart

22:55.470 --> 23:00.020
In the coldness of the locker room,

23:00.020 --> 23:06.480
Was an unfulfilled promise, locked away

23:06.990 --> 23:12.950
Dispel the darkness in this fallen world,

23:12.950 --> 23:17.500
And give me a reason why I should continue living

23:17.500 --> 23:22.880
The meaning of good-byes, the expectations of people,

23:22.880 --> 23:27.760
And the melodies that we played while never crossing paths

23:27.760 --> 23:33.470
I know I must not run away. The only path is straight ahead

23:33.470 --> 23:37.970
Even if this turns out to be a mistake

23:37.970 --> 23:43.560
The whirlpools of destiny will consume all loneliness

23:43.560 --> 23:51.660
It is an unerasable scar, an egoism that cannot be discarded

24:05.040 --> 24:10.050
Episode 12

24:05.040 --> 24:10.050
What Links Two People
